  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Study Youth Entrepreneurship in Fragile States</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is implemented in the Netherlands. The study includes case studies from Sudan and Ghana.This research project aims to investigate the role of youth entrepreneurship in uncertain and fragile settings for the Future of Work, focusing specifically on using digital solutions. The world is changing rapidly and requires us to deal with uncertainty and fragility. These developments have accelerated our use of digital solutions in the workforce and demand us to become increasingly flexible in reaching our organizational and social goals. Understanding how youth entrepreneurship plays a part in dealing with this uncertainty and fragility through digital innovation can provide insight into new ways of creating opportunities for youth and supporting the impact they are making.</narrative>
  </description>
